<section id="top" class="landing-6">
<div class="landing-7">

<h1 class="landing-8">ShadowPlay, ShareX and WizTree in one app</h1>
<p class="landing-9">Kielbox records your screen, keeps an instant replay ready, takes and annotates screenshots, trims clips and shows what is filling your disk. It is open source, and your files stay on your machine.</p>
<div class="landing-10">
<a href="https://github.com/kielerdotdev/kielbox/releases/download/preview/Kielbox-Setup.exe" class="landing-11">
<svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4"></path><polyline points="7 10 12 15 17 10"></polyline><line x1="12" x2="12" y1="15" y2="3"></line></svg>
Download for Windows</a>
<a href="https://github.com/kielerdotdev/kielbox" class="landing-12">View source</a>
</div>

</div>

<div class="landing-13"><img src="/landing/recording.png" width="1333" height="800" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high" alt="Kielbox recording the primary display: a live preview with a REC timer, instant replay, stop recording, screenshot and quick screencast controls" class="screenshot-image"></div>
</section>

<section id="why" class="landing-14">
<div class="landing-15">
<h2 class="landing-16">Why I'm building this</h2>
<div class="landing-17">
<p class="landing-18">I had a different app for every part of this, and I got tired of all of them.</p>
<p class="landing-19"><span class="landing-20">ShadowPlay</span> shut itself off every time I opened Netflix.</p>
<p class="landing-19"><span class="landing-21">ShareX</span> crashed at random. Then an update changed the interface I had learned. Then it failed to upload large files to R2.</p>
<p class="landing-19"><span class="landing-20">Medal</span> would give me clips, but then Medal has my clips. I want them as files in a folder on my disk, and when I share one, I want it on a server I run.</p>
<p class="landing-19"><span class="landing-20">WizTree</span> or <span class="landing-20">WinDirStat</span> went on every machine too, just so I could see what was eating the disk.</p>

<p class="landing-18">So Kielbox is the app I wanted: a single binary that does what I do every day, whether I'm gaming or just need a clip. Record, replay, screenshot, trim, share, find what's eating the disk. No account. Nothing leaves the machine unless I send it.</p>

<p class="landing-22">kielerdotdev</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section id="features" class="landing-14">
<div class="landing-23">
<div class="landing-24">
<h2 class="landing-25">What it does, and what it replaces</h2>
<p class="landing-26">Each of these used to be a separate install.</p>
</div>
<div class="landing-27">
<div class="landing-28">
<svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#a8a8a8" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m16 13 5.223 3.482a.5.5 0 0 0 .777-.416V7.87a.5.5 0 0 0-.752-.432L16 10.5"></path><rect x="2" y="6" width="14" height="12" rx="2"></rect></svg>
<h3 class="landing-29">Recording and instant replay</h3>
<p class="landing-30">Keep an instant replay running and save it after something happens, or record until you stop. Each audio source gets its own track.</p>

</div>
<div class="landing-28">
<svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#a8a8a8" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14.5 4h-5L7 7H4a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v9a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h16a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2h-3l-2.5-3z"></path><circle cx="12" cy="13" r="3"></circle></svg>
<h3 class="landing-29">Screenshots and annotations</h3>
<p class="landing-30">Capture a region, a window or a whole display, then add arrows, text, highlights, blur and numbered steps. You get an image plus a project you can reopen.</p>

</div>
<div class="landing-28">
<svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#a8a8a8" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="6" cy="6" r="3"></circle><path d="M8.12 8.12 12 12"></path><path d="M20 4 8.12 15.88"></path><circle cx="6" cy="18" r="3"></circle><path d="M14.8 14.8 20 20"></path></svg>
<h3 class="landing-29">Trim, edit audio, export</h3>
<p class="landing-30">Trim and split a clip, adjust its audio tracks and export a video, without opening a separate editor.</p>
</div>
<div class="landing-28">
<svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#a8a8a8" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect width="7" height="7" x="3" y="3" rx="1"></rect><rect width="7" height="7" x="14" y="3" rx="1"></rect><rect width="7" height="7" x="14" y="14" rx="1"></rect><rect width="7" height="7" x="3" y="14" rx="1"></rect></svg>
<h3 class="landing-29">A local library</h3>
<p class="landing-30">Every replay, recording and screenshot in one grid, with search, filters, favorites and video thumbnails. They are plain files in a folder you choose.</p>
</div>
<div class="landing-28">
<svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#a8a8a8" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="22" x2="2" y1="12" y2="12"></line><path d="M5.45 5.11 2 12v6a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h16a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-6l-3.45-6.89A2 2 0 0 0 16.76 4H7.24a2 2 0 0 0-1.79 1.11z"></path><line x1="6" x2="6.01" y1="16" y2="16"></line><line x1="10" x2="10.01" y1="16" y2="16"></line></svg>
<h3 class="landing-29">Disk usage</h3>
<p class="landing-30">Scan a folder and drill down to what takes the space, then reveal the file or copy its path. The scan is read-only. A separate clean command removes old node_modules and Rust build output.</p>

</div>
<div class="landing-28">
<svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#a8a8a8" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 12a9 9 0 0 1 9-9 9.75 9.75 0 0 1 6.74 2.74L21 8"></path><path d="M21 3v5h-5"></path><path d="M21 12a9 9 0 0 1-9 9 9.75 9.75 0 0 1-6.74-2.74L3 16"></path><path d="M8 16H3v5"></path></svg>
<h3 class="landing-29">Tray and updates</h3>
<p class="landing-30">Closing the window leaves Kielbox in the system tray. It checks for updates in the background, and you choose when to download and restart.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
